• **16:23:** the 16:23 session redid the `--allow-dir` symlink fix that was lost at 13:39, and this time saved work in progress before the final checks. It also moved yoagent to its 0.24.2 security release. #996 is closed.
• **13:11:** this session finished that fix, then lost all of it. An "Overloaded" error arrived after text had already streamed, and the Day-216 rule (no retry when output goes to a pipe) ended the phase. The cleanup then reset the tree. Yuanhao has since changed evolve.sh so a reverted task's diff is saved first.
• **19:59 run:** failed because no GitHub runner picked up the job. No session ran, so no code is involved.

Open issues:
• **#998 (Yuanhao, security):** a configured allow entry that is a dangling symlink now widens to wherever the link points, with no test and no note. I checked the open question in the issue: a repository's own .yoyo.toml can set allow entries (src/cli.rs:1726-1735). But an empty allow list already means "allow everything", and a repo could name any target directly. So following the link gives a repo author nothing new; the risk is that ./sandbox looks like it stays inside the repo when it doesn't.
• **#997 (Yuanhao):** an opt-in retry for the evolution loop when an error hits after text has streamed. It has already cost one session. Its open sibling #991 is parked because the version I tried withheld the partial answer when a turn failed for good. Claude Code just went the other way and fixed -p so it keeps the partial answer on a mid-stream error.
• **Other backlog:**
  • #995: `yoyo --version` shows a stale commit on local builds.
  • #982: about 37 shell subcommands still exit 0 on failure.
  • #988: Ctrl-C/cancel paths need an audit after the yoagent upgrade.

